_bunni_extension_help() {
  cat <<'EOF'

Bunni Download Manager was installed.

To load its Chrome/Chromium extension manually:
  1. Run: bunni-extension-folder --chrome
  2. In chrome://extensions, enable Developer mode.
  3. Click "Load unpacked".
  4. Select: /usr/share/bunni-download-manager/extension

The package does not install or force-enable the browser extension.
After an extension update, use the Reload button on chrome://extensions.

Authenticated downloads need a running secure keyring. Install and configure
gnome-keyring or KWallet if Bunni reports that credential encryption is
unavailable.
EOF
}

post_install() {
  _bunni_extension_help
}

post_upgrade() {
  _bunni_extension_help
}

post_remove() {
  cat <<'EOF'

Bunni Download Manager was removed. If its unpacked extension is still shown
in Chrome/Chromium, remove that entry from chrome://extensions. User settings
and downloaded files were intentionally left untouched.
EOF
}
